    <section id="faq" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>What is the best Kuvera alternative in India after the Groww acquisition?</h3>
      <p>Arthavi is the top independent Kuvera alternative for Indian investors. After Kuvera's acquisition by Groww, investors looking for an unbiased, non-broker-owned tracker use Arthavi for CAS import, family portfolio tracking, and AI-powered analytics — all free and with zero data selling.</p>

      <h3>What happened to Kuvera?</h3>
      <p>Kuvera was acquired by discount broker Groww and is being integrated into the Groww ecosystem. This means Kuvera is no longer an independent platform — it is now owned by a broker that monetizes through brokerage fees and cross-selling.</p>

      <h3>Is Arthavi independent and not owned by any broker?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Arthavi is fully independent and not affiliated with any broker, mutual fund distributor, or lending platform. It is a pure portfolio analytics tool with no conflicts of interest.</p>

      <h3>Can Arthavi track direct mutual funds like Kuvera did?</h3>
      <p>Arthavi tracks all mutual funds (direct and regular) imported through your CAS statement. Unlike Kuvera, Arthavi is a tracking-only platform and does not execute trades — keeping analytics 100% unbiased.</p>

      <h3>Does Arthavi charge any fees like Kuvera/Groww?</h3>
      <p>No. Arthavi is completely free, ad-free, and has no brokerage fees, no AUM charges, and no hidden costs. Kuvera (now Groww) monetizes through brokerage commissions on stock and mutual fund transactions.</p>
    </section>

